      "title": "TVB: make the last tvb_get function adhere to encoding enums",
      "message": "TVB: make the last tvb_get function adhere to encoding enums\n\nIt has been a long time since the boolean endianness encoding flag was\nreplaced by a more expressive bit field. This has the ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN\nvalue to indicate such encoding, among many others.\n\ntvb_get_guid() is the last of the TVB access functions that uses the\nboolean interpretation of the encoding field. Its comment suggests the\nrelated proto_tree_add_item function depends on this, but the code for\nthat function reveils the boolean interpretation of its encoding flag\nis already made there and replaced with ENC_LITTLE_ENDIAN if needed.\n\nTherefore both the comment can be dropped and the expression aligned\nwith the other TVB access functions.\n",
